  "minimum_safe_summary": "This empirical study investigates the impact of interventions on anxiety and academic performance. One study found that a positive psychology-based intervention significantly reduced anxiety (SAS scores) in staff compared to a control group. Another study, based on educational psychology theory, demonstrated that incorporating a practice link in an environmental psychology course significantly decreased learning anxiety (SDS scores) and improved academic performance in architectural design students compared to a traditional teaching approach. The paper does not explicitly state any limitations.",
